{"title":"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> is a square with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> are on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/805452ee372321839953fbd750cd9b23b973a3df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> respectively with\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1a8b0221d229a20dfa9c2a126c1c52ba7c39af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QU = TS = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />. The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/5/3e5abc1dc130c799e3e731edb03d65b259503fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is closest to\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/8/58848b60265130547fc5164acfcc800b44625e08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\   8.5 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\   9.9 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\   10 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\   10.6 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\   11.3 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"468\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can make a line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c76efdaa02d0ad4ec091a4e19dfb105ad45492e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TV$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c52aff9dd9987076c0ac4fecccf59b6ed8bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/8/6a89bdd4e47d61463a262dafcc0bbb4e25160470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TVRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> is a rectangle.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/8/6a89bdd4e47d61463a262dafcc0bbb4e25160470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TVRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> is a rectangle, opposite sides in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/8/6a89bdd4e47d61463a262dafcc0bbb4e25160470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TVRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> are equal, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49ec1c3f8d04228a72cd6ac48631ebb7079e0b2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TS = RV = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df65b8327fc3e41add6394c946925e0099b41bf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS = TV = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e87148d94cfc177efc6315d18c0f5617f901900b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR = QU + RV + UV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/5027c7ebf52bc11177bd92526b1a59f6806e75a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 = 1 + 1 + UV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"16\" />. This gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/3/2732aa4933ba1bfb7f3993294838d06f1f9a3f69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$UV = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The angles in a rectangle are all equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, so we can use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">pythagorean theorem</a> to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/5/3e5abc1dc130c799e3e731edb03d65b259503fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/25310aae8b4e4580d235d19b06877e914e055718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TU^{2} = TV^{2} + UV^{2} = 8^{2} + 6^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"235\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/246f3c8116db35e5be1bd2330c3c6ea05a99b31b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TU^{2} = 64 + 36 = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a857d0ffdc3f9cf924c6ca9d50607d1ff81ae2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TU = \\sqrt{100} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"185\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>We could have also realized that the legs were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times that of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> right triangle, so the hypotenuse would have to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/dae2bfd3d5a54e4c853891ca1c7a6d8a61175e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 5 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"131\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat\">2014 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</